WEBVTT

01:01.861 --> 01:03.829
Lovely day for a walk, eh, Holmes?

01:03.830 --> 01:07.165
Yes, just look at our great
city, bustling with activity.

01:07.166 --> 01:09.668
Even the chimney sweeps
are hard at work.

01:09.669 --> 01:11.370
It's all dirty in here.

01:11.371 --> 01:13.105
I don't care. Keep going.

01:13.106 --> 01:15.607
Shouldn't I wear
some sort of protective suit?

01:15.608 --> 01:17.442
Why? Don't you trust me?

01:17.443 --> 01:20.812
I do, but our friend Bartholomew
went in lots of chimneys

01:20.813 --> 01:23.714
in the '80s, and now he's sick.

01:27.487 --> 01:29.855
Holmes, there's something
I have to tell you.

01:29.856 --> 01:31.456
- I'm getting married...
- I deduce, Watson,

01:31.457 --> 01:33.025
- that you're getting married.
- I just said that.

01:33.026 --> 01:34.192
Yes, but I had deduced it first.

01:34.193 --> 01:35.260
That's what happened.

01:35.261 --> 01:36.361
So, congratulations.

01:36.362 --> 01:37.529
Thank you.

01:37.530 --> 01:38.797
I thought you might be upset

01:38.798 --> 01:40.198
because we won't be able
to solve mysteries...

01:40.199 --> 01:41.400
Solve mysteries together.

01:41.401 --> 01:42.734
Elementary.

01:42.735 --> 01:44.202
Crown Jewels stolen!

01:44.203 --> 01:46.638
"Another one bites the dust,"
says Queen.

01:46.639 --> 01:48.540
And coming up, Russia and Prussia

01:48.541 --> 01:51.410
still named basically the same thing.

01:51.411 --> 01:54.413
Ghastly. Who would have
the audacity to steal the crown

01:54.414 --> 01:55.914
off the queen's head?

01:55.915 --> 01:57.616
Only one man, Watson.

01:57.617 --> 02:00.485
Professor Moriarty,
the Napoleon of Crime.

02:00.486 --> 02:02.487
I've had him on the run for a year now.

02:02.488 --> 02:04.189
His criminal empire is in shambles,

02:04.190 --> 02:05.590
but he won't go quietly.

02:05.591 --> 02:08.694
I say, look, there's hotshot
20-year-old comedian

02:08.695 --> 02:10.195
Benjamin Hill.

02:14.467 --> 02:18.136
Oh. That'll be funnier
when he's older and slower.

02:22.275 --> 02:24.810
Watson, this is the boat to America.

02:24.811 --> 02:25.978
How do you know that?

02:25.979 --> 02:28.480
Because Neil Diamond is on board. Look.

02:28.481 --> 02:31.183
♪ September morn ♪

02:31.184 --> 02:35.821
♪ We danced until the night
became a brand-new day... ♪

02:35.822 --> 02:37.856
I really hoped
he'd be singing "America."

02:37.857 --> 02:39.658
Well, how will we know who Moriarty is?

02:39.659 --> 02:40.892
We've never seen him before.

02:40.893 --> 02:42.627
The science of deduction.

02:42.628 --> 02:44.595
Hold it right there, Professor Moriarty.

02:46.032 --> 02:47.366
Sherlock Holmes?

02:47.367 --> 02:48.867
How did you know it was me?

02:48.868 --> 02:51.103
When I see a man
about to go on a sea voyage

02:51.104 --> 02:52.504
and not wearing a topcoat,

02:52.505 --> 02:55.674
with no watch fob, and whose
spats are not fully buttoned...

02:55.675 --> 02:58.210
And the jewels hanging out of my hat?

02:58.211 --> 02:59.844
Yeah, and the jewels
hanging out of your hat.

03:02.515 --> 03:04.850
He's got a gun.
Look out, Stew... Holmes!

03:04.851 --> 03:06.351
God, this is gonna be so annoying.

03:06.352 --> 03:07.652
Watson, the scepter!

03:10.523 --> 03:12.357
Aah! Lucky shot.

03:12.358 --> 03:13.959
There was no luck involved.

03:13.960 --> 03:15.494
From the angle you were aiming the gun,

03:15.495 --> 03:17.295
I extrapolated the path of the bullet,

03:17.296 --> 03:19.231
and triangulated the deflection point...

03:19.232 --> 03:21.166
Uh, is this... is this speech for me?

03:21.167 --> 03:22.566
Because he's dead.

03:30.977 --> 03:32.277
For the court's amusement,

03:32.278 --> 03:35.714
we now present Sir William of Cosby.

03:35.715 --> 03:38.383
Well, you see, the children
of today are wearing

03:38.384 --> 03:40.852
their pantaloons so low, gazoozle,

03:40.853 --> 03:43.855
you can see the first three
layers of their undergarments,

03:43.856 --> 03:45.222
zazzle, zoozle.

03:48.995 --> 03:53.198
I get away with this
for another 122 years, you see.

03:53.199 --> 03:56.435
Hello, Your Majesty, I have
recovered the Crown Jewels.

03:56.436 --> 03:58.770
Mum, may I say, it's been
a pleasure serving you,

03:58.771 --> 04:00.405
but I've decided to retire.

04:00.406 --> 04:03.375
We are losing interest
in this conversation.

04:03.376 --> 04:06.745
It would be a wonderful cap on
my career to have a knighthood.

04:06.746 --> 04:09.014
Come, come, now, Holmes, you're not...

04:10.516 --> 04:12.284
Sometimes the bigger ladies

04:12.285 --> 04:14.885
take a little longer, you see.

04:27.433 --> 04:29.301
Really, Holmes, why retire?

04:29.302 --> 04:31.136
There will still be crimes to solve.

04:31.137 --> 04:33.772
But with Moriarty gone,
and with you, my biographer,

04:33.773 --> 04:36.408
leaving me for marriage,
there is little point.

04:36.409 --> 04:38.610
Just gonna toss it in the old waste bin.

04:38.611 --> 04:40.946
Yup. Good-bye, detective cap.

04:40.947 --> 04:42.913
Yeah.

04:45.084 --> 04:48.086
And you, old chap, are about
to solve the biggest mystery

04:48.087 --> 04:50.922
facing men of our time:
the wedding night.

04:50.923 --> 04:53.758
I know, I'm just, I'm just giddy
with anticipation.

04:53.759 --> 04:56.695
Lifting her nightgown,
nightshirt, evening cape,

04:56.696 --> 04:58.930
boudoir coverall, torso doily,

04:58.931 --> 05:01.233
and the various corsets
and trusses below.

05:01.234 --> 05:03.068
Exposing her shame to God,

05:03.069 --> 05:06.071
followed by brief missionary
coitus with no eye contact.

05:06.072 --> 05:07.572
And then, five months later,

05:07.573 --> 05:10.242
a stillborn child
the size of a digestive biscuit.

05:13.279 --> 05:14.446
Constance.

05:14.447 --> 05:17.315
John.

05:17.316 --> 05:19.017
- Hey.
- 'Sup?

05:19.018 --> 05:21.486
So, my betrothed,
how go the wedding plans?

05:21.487 --> 05:24.122
Oh, John, my father
is sparing no expense.

05:24.123 --> 05:27.726
Boiled beef for every guest,
fish head stew, old cheese,

05:27.727 --> 05:29.394
and men's attire will be provided

05:29.395 --> 05:31.029
by Gentlemen's Wearhouse.

05:31.030 --> 05:34.765
You're gonna fancy the way
you look, this I vouchsafe.

05:36.102 --> 05:37.135
What is it, Holmes?

05:37.136 --> 05:38.236
It's an urgent missive

05:38.237 --> 05:40.505
from Inspector Lestrade
of Scotland Yard.

05:40.506 --> 05:43.842
Oh, darn, there's been a murder
and he's begging for my help.

05:43.843 --> 05:46.945
Oh, darn, darn, darn,
this is embarrassing.

05:46.946 --> 05:50.248
Now I've got to see if I can
dig that hat out of the trash.

05:50.249 --> 05:52.316
Come, Watson, the game is afoot.

05:53.386 --> 05:54.519
"Afoot"?

05:54.520 --> 05:56.021
"Starting," "beginning."

05:56.022 --> 05:58.123
Well, then just say that.

05:58.124 --> 05:59.891
Enjoying all the old-timey jokes?

05:59.892 --> 06:03.427
Don't worry, next week,
back to a normal episode.

06:08.501 --> 06:10.835
Hmm, this is most curious.

06:10.836 --> 06:14.506
It appears she was killed by our
old nemesis, the Scottish Brute.

06:14.507 --> 06:16.241
That's impossible, he's in prison.

06:16.242 --> 06:18.043
I put him there myself one year ago.

06:18.044 --> 06:20.412
Nevertheless,
we can't ignore the evidence.

06:20.413 --> 06:22.113
All his victims were prostitutes

06:22.114 --> 06:23.915
whose names began with the letter "V."

06:23.916 --> 06:26.551
This one's name is Veronica,
as evidenced

06:26.552 --> 06:30.388
by this satin softball jacket
that bears her name.

06:30.389 --> 06:33.258
These threads are from
a Scotsman's plaid kilt.

06:33.259 --> 06:36.194
The telltale locks of red hair.

06:36.195 --> 06:39.197
But most significantly,
the Scottish Brute replaced

06:39.198 --> 06:42.067
his victims' intestines with bagpipes.

06:43.869 --> 06:45.470
Want to give it a whirl?

06:58.417 --> 07:00.418
How could he accomplish
this murder from prison?

07:00.419 --> 07:01.586
He couldn't.

07:01.587 --> 07:03.989
There are only
two possible explanations:

07:03.990 --> 07:06.057
either there's a murderer who has copied

07:06.058 --> 07:10.227
the Scottish Brute's methods,
or I put the wrong man away.

07:22.308 --> 07:23.775
What are you in for?

07:23.776 --> 07:26.578
Ah, I Rathboned somebody's Cumberbatch.

07:35.921 --> 07:37.455
Well, well, well.

07:37.456 --> 07:40.425
If it ain't me old nemesis,
Sherlock Holmes.

07:40.426 --> 07:42.427
Hello, Brute, I've got
some questions for you.

07:42.428 --> 07:44.496
Who did you tell about the murders?

07:44.497 --> 07:47.365
Nae a soul, 'cause I dinna
commit no murders.

07:47.366 --> 07:49.134
I'm innocent, you nosy parker.

07:49.135 --> 07:50.302
How can I believe you?

07:50.303 --> 07:51.770
You're a common criminal.

07:51.771 --> 07:55.440
All the prostitutes were killed
by a left-handed assailant.

07:55.441 --> 07:57.876
- So?
- So, I was born with...

07:57.877 --> 07:59.644
two right hands.

07:59.645 --> 08:01.346
Dear God.

08:01.347 --> 08:03.448
That means he couldn't
have been the killer.

08:03.449 --> 08:07.385
That's right. You ever seen
a man with two right hand...

08:07.386 --> 08:09.120
Oh, this... this thing was open.

08:09.121 --> 08:10.455
That shouldn't be open, right?

08:10.456 --> 08:12.084
No, no, I wouldn't think so.

08:19.618 --> 08:22.286
I hope you will accept
my sincere apologies.

08:22.287 --> 08:24.755
Oh, you've done more than
made up for it, Mr. Holmes.

08:24.756 --> 08:26.557
I'm just happy to be free.

08:26.558 --> 08:28.993
Ah, the world's changed
since I've been in there.

08:28.994 --> 08:30.961
That puddle wasn't here.

08:30.962 --> 08:32.596
That cloud wasn't there.

08:32.597 --> 08:34.432
That window was open.

08:34.433 --> 08:36.667
That lady was four feet that way.

08:36.668 --> 08:38.402
All right, well, I hope
you make a go of it.

08:38.403 --> 08:40.104
Good luck with your fresh start.

08:40.105 --> 08:42.540
Oh, where'd that bird come from?

08:42.541 --> 08:44.007
That's new.

08:48.713 --> 08:51.549
Watson, I found
some important new clues.

08:51.550 --> 08:53.984
These red locks of hair
I found at the crime scene?

08:53.985 --> 08:55.953
They don't belong to the Scottish Brute.

08:55.954 --> 08:57.655
They belong to a woman.

08:57.656 --> 08:58.656
How can you tell?

08:58.657 --> 09:00.057
It's hard to explain, Watson.

09:00.058 --> 09:01.525
Women are mysterious.

09:01.526 --> 09:02.793
But don't ask me.

09:02.794 --> 09:05.963
Ask contemporary personality
Oscar Wilde.

09:05.964 --> 09:10.734
I prefer a man with a future
and a woman with a past.

09:10.735 --> 09:11.936
Oh, splendid.

09:11.937 --> 09:13.804
Well said, splendid.

09:13.805 --> 09:15.673
All right, let's get out of here
before we're all arrested

09:15.674 --> 09:18.174
for the crime of "bum-fancy."

09:20.846 --> 09:25.416
And now I will disguise myself
as a prostitute named Valerie.

09:25.417 --> 09:26.817
What the devil is that?

09:26.818 --> 09:28.052
It's my own invention.

09:28.053 --> 09:30.187
A steam-driven mechanical exoskeleton.

09:30.188 --> 09:31.488
Observe.

09:36.228 --> 09:39.430
It's cutting-edge technology, Watson!

09:39.431 --> 09:41.031
Exchange money

09:41.032 --> 09:43.067
for sexual services, guv'nor.

09:43.068 --> 09:44.135
Are you a bobby?

09:44.136 --> 09:45.236
You have to tell me.

09:45.237 --> 09:46.504
Mind the gap.

09:46.505 --> 09:47.938
Astounding.

09:47.939 --> 09:50.274
Yes. Now, I'll stroll around the block,

09:50.275 --> 09:53.444
and you'll proposition me, loud
enough so the killer can hear.

09:53.445 --> 09:54.912
Love for sale.

09:54.913 --> 09:57.515
Appetizing young love for sale.

09:57.516 --> 09:59.817
♪ Love that's fresh
and still unspoiled ♪

09:59.818 --> 10:02.253
♪ Love that's only slightly soiled... ♪

10:02.254 --> 10:03.387
Love for sale.

10:03.388 --> 10:04.555
Lookin' good, honey.

10:04.556 --> 10:05.656
No blacks.

10:05.657 --> 10:07.057
Love for sale.

10:07.058 --> 10:09.692
Race-contingent love for sale.

10:16.434 --> 10:19.537
Did I hear your name was Valerie?

10:19.538 --> 10:20.771
Yeah, guv'nor.

10:20.772 --> 10:21.939
Uh, have we met?

10:21.940 --> 10:24.240
Your voice sounds very familiar.

10:33.051 --> 10:34.652
What the hell is this?

10:34.653 --> 10:35.853
Watson, hurry!

10:35.854 --> 10:37.087
Watson?

10:37.088 --> 10:38.656
Oh, my God, Sherlock!

10:38.657 --> 10:41.559
Watson, help.

10:41.560 --> 10:43.326
Watson.

10:45.363 --> 10:49.200
All I would've done
is be a perfect gentleman.

10:49.201 --> 10:50.868
Sorry, got distracted.

10:50.869 --> 10:52.970
Lot of rats in London.

10:52.971 --> 10:54.437
That's for you.

10:58.210 --> 11:00.077
Sorry we didn't
catch the murderer, Holmes.

11:00.078 --> 11:02.112
And I'm afraid you'll
have to catch her without me.

11:02.113 --> 11:03.414
My wedding is tomorrow.

11:03.415 --> 11:05.082
Yes, about that, you know,
I was thinking.

11:05.083 --> 11:07.184
Maybe you should put that off
for a little while.

11:07.185 --> 11:09.320
You know, sow a few more wild oats.

11:09.321 --> 11:10.955
Oh, I've done enough of that, my friend,

11:10.956 --> 11:13.157
especially after that
raucous bachelor party trip

11:13.158 --> 11:15.024
you threw for me in Las Vegas.

11:17.696 --> 11:20.097
So... when do the strippers arrive?

11:20.098 --> 11:22.333
1952.

11:22.334 --> 11:25.369
Watson, I don't know
how to tell you this...

11:25.370 --> 11:28.005
but the murderer
we've been looking for...

11:28.006 --> 11:29.773
it's your fiancГ©e, Constance.

11:29.774 --> 11:31.875
You lie! You're just jealous!

11:31.876 --> 11:33.978
Well, let's go to her place
and I'll show you.

11:33.979 --> 11:36.947
Sorry, today was y'all's cleaning day.

11:36.948 --> 11:38.782
Y'all want me to come back later?

11:38.783 --> 11:40.117
M-Maybe, maybe, yeah.

11:40.118 --> 11:41.518
M-Maybe, maybe another day.

11:41.519 --> 11:43.153
That's fine, I'll pull out.

11:43.154 --> 11:45.990
Just go easy,
it really hurt on the way in.

11:45.991 --> 11:48.692
Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow!

11:48.693 --> 11:50.627
Ow! Ow! Ow!

11:54.933 --> 11:58.202
Constance? Are you here?

11:58.203 --> 12:01.105
She's... she's gone.

12:01.106 --> 12:03.040
I'm sorry, Watson. Unfortunately,

12:03.041 --> 12:05.175
it appears my deductions were correct.

12:05.176 --> 12:07.278
Not so fast. Look, she left a note.

12:07.279 --> 12:09.179
See, Holmes? It says here...

12:09.180 --> 12:11.915
these are test results.
She has gonorrhea.

12:11.916 --> 12:13.350
I...

12:13.351 --> 12:15.019
I can't believe it.

12:15.020 --> 12:17.221
My beloved Constance is the murderer.

12:17.222 --> 12:18.789
It's even worse than you think.

12:18.790 --> 12:21.125
If she's a murderer
from this time period,

12:21.126 --> 12:23.694
that means there will be
a terrible, pretentious musical

12:23.695 --> 12:25.329
about her one day.

12:27.732 --> 12:30.301
♪ Behold the tale of Constance ♪

12:30.302 --> 12:32.836
♪ The murderer in the bonnet ♪

12:32.837 --> 12:36.707
<i>♪ The murderer in the bonnet. ♪</i>

12:36.708 --> 12:39.043
Oh, I was wrong, I love it.

12:39.044 --> 12:40.377
<i>Will Watson and Holmes</i>

12:40.378 --> 12:41.845
<i>track down Constance?</i>

12:41.846 --> 12:43.147
<i>We'll be right back</i>

12:43.148 --> 12:45.449
<i>after these
turn of the century messages.</i>

12:45.450 --> 12:49.286
Another dull night
at the gentlemen's club.

12:49.287 --> 12:51.989
What we need is
some room temperature gin.

12:51.990 --> 12:53.424
'Ello, gents.

12:53.425 --> 12:55.659
Fancy some Room Temperature Gin?

12:55.660 --> 12:57.061
Shut up, you slag!

12:57.062 --> 12:58.495
No women allowed.

12:58.496 --> 13:00.197
<i>Room Temperature Gin:</i>

13:00.198 --> 13:01.465
<i>drink it without women,</i>

13:01.466 --> 13:03.266
<i>have an eel pie, then go to bed.</i>

13:09.133 --> 13:12.102
Constance had the tickets
for our honeymoon to Paris.

13:12.103 --> 13:14.004
No doubt she'll be using those
for her escape.

13:14.005 --> 13:15.705
Very well. Then we're off to France.

13:15.706 --> 13:18.175
That's right. We're off to Gay Paree.

13:18.176 --> 13:20.010
- What's this now?
- Gay Paree.

13:20.011 --> 13:21.511
Some... some people call it "Gay Paree."

13:21.512 --> 13:23.913
Oh, then I suppose I should change.

13:25.950 --> 13:29.786
Let's get separate rooms just so
we can spread our stuff out.

13:36.827 --> 13:38.328
Quick, we've got to catch the train!

13:38.329 --> 13:40.329
Porter!

13:42.166 --> 13:43.900
Watson, do you have thruppence
for the porter?

13:43.901 --> 13:45.068
I have tuppence.

13:45.069 --> 13:46.203
So you don't have thruppence?

13:46.204 --> 13:47.904
I have tuppence. How much do you have?

13:47.905 --> 13:49.072
I have nuppence.

13:49.073 --> 13:50.807
You're gonna get a comeuppance.

13:57.014 --> 13:59.783
Excuse me, sir, what's the next
stop for this train?

14:01.652 --> 14:04.654
Ugh, I hate when they let
the infirm ride on the train.

14:04.655 --> 14:08.558
Next stop, (BABBLING) Station.

14:08.559 --> 14:12.028
Sir, you owe an apology to me
and all the good people

14:12.029 --> 14:15.498
of (BABBLING).

14:15.499 --> 14:19.069
It's nice of the locals to act
as their own train crossings.

14:19.070 --> 14:22.037
Ding, ding, ding, ding, ding,
ding, ding, ding, ding.

14:30.514 --> 14:32.515
You know, I've never crossed
the English Channel before.

14:32.516 --> 14:34.251
I hope no one from the train
is on this boat.

14:34.252 --> 14:35.418
I'm wearing the same outfit.

14:35.419 --> 14:36.786
I wouldn't worry.

14:36.787 --> 14:39.189
Looks like it's just a bunch
of minor celebrities.

14:48.966 --> 14:50.766
♪ Love ♪

14:52.703 --> 14:56.740
♪ Exciting and new ♪

14:56.741 --> 14:58.208
♪ Come aboard. ♪

15:04.215 --> 15:06.182
Finally, Paris.

15:06.183 --> 15:07.884
What an ordeal.

15:07.885 --> 15:09.219
Yes, but how do we find Constance

15:09.220 --> 15:10.387
in one of the biggest cities...

15:10.388 --> 15:11.688
There she is.

15:13.257 --> 15:14.858
Quick, after her. We have to chase her

15:14.859 --> 15:16.393
through a series of shots where she has

15:16.394 --> 15:18.728
an inconsistent lead on us.

15:46.290 --> 15:47.457
This way, Holmes.

15:47.458 --> 15:49.225
She's heading towards... Holmes?

15:49.226 --> 15:51.728
I couldn't come here and not do this.

15:51.729 --> 15:54.063
She has appendicitis, by the way.

15:59.270 --> 16:00.670
She must have gone up
this strange building.

16:00.671 --> 16:01.805
What is it?

16:01.806 --> 16:03.239
It's the brand-new Eiffel Tower.

16:03.240 --> 16:04.507
Well, let's hurry.

16:04.508 --> 16:06.142
- She's getting...
- Oh, oh, hold on, hold on.

16:06.143 --> 16:07.477
I think we may have just photobombed

16:07.478 --> 16:08.778
that family's picture.

16:25.830 --> 16:27.664
You'll never catch me.

16:29.166 --> 16:31.300
Damn it, my heel is caught.

16:34.171 --> 16:35.471
Constance!

16:36.607 --> 16:37.774
Hang on, my darling.

16:37.775 --> 16:41.111
John, I did it for him.

16:41.112 --> 16:43.146
And you didn't mean to hurt me?

16:43.147 --> 16:45.348
No, you're not getting what I'm saying.

16:45.349 --> 16:47.684
I didn't care about you at all.

16:47.685 --> 16:49.119
Who did you do this for?

16:49.120 --> 16:51.621
Why were you killing prostitutes
with the initial "V"?

16:52.957 --> 16:54.858
The great Sherlock Holmes.

16:54.859 --> 16:56.860
He said you'd never figure it out,

16:56.861 --> 16:59.162
and that he'd be victorious.

17:03.033 --> 17:04.200
Constance!

17:08.205 --> 17:11.508
Ugh. Depardieu!

17:17.014 --> 17:20.016
I can't believe she's gone, Holmes.

17:20.017 --> 17:21.418
Oh, you'll find someone.

17:21.419 --> 17:23.153
You're a good guy with a great body.

17:23.154 --> 17:24.821
I still don't understand what she meant

17:24.822 --> 17:27.190
by "he said you'd never
figure it out, and..."

17:27.191 --> 17:28.691
"That he'd be victorious."

17:28.692 --> 17:30.360
Watson, that's it.

17:30.361 --> 17:32.162
Didn't think I'd figure it out.

17:32.163 --> 17:35.565
This calls for the old Sherlock
Holmes celebratory smoke.

17:35.566 --> 17:37.032
I'll just light my pipe.

17:59.857 --> 18:01.958
What is the meaning of this?

18:01.959 --> 18:03.960
I'll be replacing your innards

18:03.961 --> 18:06.229
with these bagpipes, Queen Victoria.

18:06.230 --> 18:09.132
Not before we put you in jail.

18:09.133 --> 18:10.333
What's with this "we" crap?

18:10.334 --> 18:11.468
It's just you.

18:11.469 --> 18:15.371
Oh, no, it's "we."

18:16.473 --> 18:18.675
We made it just in time.

18:18.676 --> 18:21.978
And I was able to fool you,
as I am a master of disguise.

18:21.979 --> 18:24.547
Seems like you're just good
at dressing up like a woman.

18:24.548 --> 18:26.449
Ah, you caught me, Mr. Holmes.

18:26.450 --> 18:28.585
I suppose it's back to jail for me.

18:28.586 --> 18:32.121
You can dispense with the act,
Professor Moriarty.

18:32.122 --> 18:33.456
Holmes, what are you talking about?

18:33.457 --> 18:35.091
Moriarty's dead. You killed him.

18:35.092 --> 18:37.026
No, that was one of his lackeys.

18:37.027 --> 18:38.962
Isn't that right, Professor?

18:38.963 --> 18:40.763
Very clever, Holmes.

18:40.764 --> 18:42.298
What gave me away?

18:42.299 --> 18:45.602
Constance. She said
that you'd be victorious.

18:45.603 --> 18:47.136
That was the vital clue

18:47.137 --> 18:49.572
that these murders were for my benefit.

18:49.573 --> 18:51.908
<i>I was dismantling your criminal empire,</i>

18:51.909 --> 18:53.408
<i>and you wanted revenge.</i>

19:01.619 --> 19:04.387
You cannot catch what you cannot see.

19:07.091 --> 19:10.093
<i>So, you concocted
an elaborate series of murders</i>

19:10.094 --> 19:11.194
<i>with clues leading me</i>

19:11.195 --> 19:13.263
<i>to the fictional Scottish Brute.</i>

19:13.264 --> 19:15.598
<i>Meanwhile, two toothless,
British homeless people</i>

19:15.599 --> 19:17.467
<i>had filthy sex in an alleyway.</i>

19:17.468 --> 19:19.002
<i>They would become the grandparents</i>

19:19.003 --> 19:20.569
<i>of the guys from Oasis.</i>

19:23.173 --> 19:25.108
<i>Meanwhile, you had your girlfriend</i>

19:25.109 --> 19:26.608
<i>seduce my best friend.</i>

19:32.449 --> 19:34.216
<i>She arranges for me
to kill your imposter...</i>

19:35.352 --> 19:37.921
<i>and commits an identical murder</i>

19:37.922 --> 19:40.890
so I would come
to the inescapable conclusion

19:40.891 --> 19:42.559
that I put the wrong man away.

19:42.560 --> 19:44.627
Constance would lead us
away from England

19:44.628 --> 19:46.829
while you killed the last "prostitute"

19:46.830 --> 19:48.131
with the name "V."

19:48.132 --> 19:49.966
And I'd get the blame
for freeing the man

19:49.967 --> 19:51.834
who killed our beloved queen.

19:51.835 --> 19:53.069
Brilliant.

19:53.070 --> 19:55.238
Why do you think
Queen Victoria's a prostitute?

19:55.239 --> 19:57.073
She formed an alliance
with the Dutch royals

19:57.074 --> 19:59.142
for shared control of Guyana.

19:59.143 --> 20:00.810
So... political.

20:00.811 --> 20:02.912
One last mystery to solve.

20:02.913 --> 20:04.847
Why do they call you Professor?

20:04.848 --> 20:06.683
- I teach at Hogwarts.
- Really?

20:06.684 --> 20:09.819
No. But we should've done that
instead of this.

20:13.824 --> 20:15.858
Holmes, with this case,

20:15.859 --> 20:17.961
you saved the entire British Empire.

20:17.962 --> 20:20.129
Yes. Now it will last forever.

20:20.130 --> 20:22.231
From South Africa to the Suez Canal,

20:22.232 --> 20:23.933
from Cyprus to Australia,

20:23.934 --> 20:25.802
all of Canada and Grenada,

20:25.803 --> 20:28.571
even Antigua and Jamaica.

20:28.572 --> 20:30.473
India, Jordan, Kenya, Kuwait,

20:30.474 --> 20:32.508
Malawi, Bermuda, the Falklands.

20:32.509 --> 20:34.710
Yes, all part of our empire.

20:36.513 --> 20:37.814
I'll always miss...

20:37.815 --> 20:39.082
<i>The Maldives, Myanmar,</i>

20:39.083 --> 20:41.050
<i>New Zealand, Nigeria, Pakistan.</i>

20:41.051 --> 20:42.785
<i>Saint Kitts and Nevis.</i>

20:42.786 --> 20:44.754
<i>Sri Lanka, the Sudan, Uganda,</i>

20:44.755 --> 20:46.422
<i>and the United Arab Emirates.</i>

20:46.423 --> 20:48.358
<i>God, England sucks now.</i>

20:51.325 --> 20:54.825
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru